# .gitleaksignore — fingerprints intentionally excluded from secret scanning.
#
# Format: one gitleaks Fingerprint per line, in the form `commit:file:rule:line`. gitleaks
# reads this file itself when its --source (or --repo-path) is this repo's own root — nothing
# in agent/lib/secrets_scan.py needs to know this file exists; see
# tests/test_secrets_scan.py::test_run_secrets_scan_does_not_need_to_know_about_gitleaksignore.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo's own test suite intentionally plants fake-looking
# credential strings to prove the secrets engine finds them (drift-detector-scan is a
# scanner whose tests have to contain scanner-shaped bait). Left unaddressed, those
# fixtures would surface as findings every time this repo scans itself in CI. This file
# exists ONLY to silence that self-inflicted noise — it must NEVER be used to suppress a
# real, unrotated leak, in this repo or (obviously) in any fleet repo this tool scans on
# someone else's behalf; a real key sitting in a vendored file elsewhere is still a real leak.
#
